" name=\"query\" id=\"arxiv-search-input\" autocomplete=\"off\"\n85\t        placeholder=\"Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...\">\n86\t      <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"searchtype\" value=\"all\">\n87\t      <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"source\" value=\"header\">\n88\t    </form>\n89\t    <div class=\"arxiv-search-hint\">\n90\t      Press Enter to search &middot; <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/advanced\">Advanced search</a>\n91\t    </div>\n92\t  </div>\n93\t</div>\n94\t    <main>\n95\t      <div id=\"content\">\n96\t<!--\n97\trdf:RDF xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\"\n98\t         xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\"\n99\t         xmlns:trackback=\"http://madskills.com/public/xml/rss/module/trackback/\">\n100\t    <rdf:Description\n101\t        rdf:about=\"/abs/2608.06198\"\n102\t        dc:identifier=\"/abs/2608.06198\"\n103\t        dc:title=\"Numerical Model of a Multiple-Input-Multiple-Output Distributed Acoustic Sensing System with Joint Phase and Birefringence Estimation\"\n104\t        trackback:ping=\"/trackback/2608.06198\" />\n105\t    </rdf:RDF>\n106\t--><div id=\"abs-outer\">\n107\t\n108\t  <div class=\"leftcolumn\">\n109\t    <div class=\"subheader\">\n110\t      <h1>Electrical Engineering and Systems Science > Signal Processing</h1>\n111\t    </div>\n112\t\n113\t    <div class=\"header-breadcrumbs-mobile\">\n114\t      <strong>arXiv:2608.06198v1</strong> (eess)\n115\t    </div>\n116\t<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"/static/base/1.0.1/css/abs.css\">\n117\t<div id=\"content-inner\">\n118\t  <div id=\"abs\">\n119\t    <div class=\"dateline\">\n120\t  [Submitted on 6 Aug 2026]</div>\n121\t    <h1 class=\"title mathjax\"><span class=\"descriptor\">Title:</span>Numerical Model of a Multiple-Input-Multiple-Output Distributed Acoustic Sensing System with Joint Phase and Birefringence Estimation</h1>\n122\t    <div class=\"authors\"><span class=\"descriptor\">Authors:</span><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/eess?searchtype=author&amp;query=Prato,+D\" rel=\"nofollow\">Diane Prato</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/eess?searchtype=author&amp;query=Sheramin,+M+M\" rel=\"nofollow\">Mehran Mokhtari Sheramin</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/eess?searchtype=author&amp;query=Gabet,+R\" rel=\"nofollow\">Renaud Gabet</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/eess?searchtype=author&amp;query=Awwad,+E\" rel=\"nofollow\">Elie Awwad</a></div>            <div id=\"download-button-info\" hidden>View a PDF of the paper titled Numerical Model of a Multiple-Input-Multiple-Output Distributed Acoustic Sensing System with Joint Phase and Birefringence Estimation, by Diane Prato and 3 other authors</div>\n123\t    <a class=\"mobile-submission-download\" href=\"/pdf/2608.06198v1\">View PDF</a>\n124\t    <a class=\"mobile-submission-download\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2608.06198v1\">HTML (experimental)</a>\n125\t\n126\t\n127\t\n128\t    <blockquote class=\"abstract mathjax\">\n129\t            <span class=\"descriptor\">Abstract:</span>In this work, we introduce and experimentally validate a numerical model for a Multiple-Input-Multiple-Output Distributed Acoustic Sensing (MIMO-DAS) system that accounts for dynamic perturbations of fiber birefringence and of the common optical phase of the backscattered signal (or polarization-averaged phase, shared by both polarization tributaries). The MIMO-DAS system probes the fiber using polarization-multiplexed constant-power coded sequences that are suited for coexistence of DAS with WDM data transmission over the same fiber. We study the effect of both axisymmetric and anisotropic events on the two quantities. We demonstrate, through numerical simulations and lab experiments, the estimation of effective birefringence magnitude in static conditions, and the joint estimation of common phase and effective birefringence magnitude in the case of dynamic longitudinal strain and anisotropic transverse strain. This allows for event discrimination and increased sensitivity to disturbances that act transversely on the fiber, since polarization will be responsive to perturbations that break cylindrical symmetry, while the phase will strongly respond to longitudinal strain.\n130\t    </blockquote>\n131\t\n132\t    <!--CONTEXT-->\n133\t    <div class=\"metatable\">\n134\t      <table summary=\"Additional metadata\"><tr>\n135\t          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Subjects:</td>\n136\t          <td class=\"tablecell subjects\">\n137\t            <span class=\"primary-subject\">Signal Processing (eess.SP)</span>; Optics (physics.optics)</td>\n138\t        </tr><tr>\n139\t          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Cite as:</td>\n140\t          <td class=\"tablecell arxivid\"><span class=\"arxivid\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.06198\">arXiv:2608.06198</a> [eess.SP]</span></td>\n141\t        </tr>\n142\t        <tr>\n143\t          <td class=\"tablecell label\">&nbsp;</td>\n144\t          <td class=\"tablecell arxividv\">(or <span class=\"arxivid\">\n145\t              <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.06198v1\">arXiv:2608.06198v1</a> [eess.SP]</span> for this version)\n146\t          </td>\n147\t        </tr>\n148\t        <tr>\n149\t          <td class=\"tablecell label\">&nbsp;</td>\n150\t          <td class=\"tablecell arxivdoi\">              <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2608.06198\" id=\"arxiv-doi-link\">https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2608.06198</a><div class=\"button-and-tooltip\">\n151\t              <button class=\"more-info\" aria-describedby=\"more-info-desc-1\">\n152\t                <svg height=\"15\" role=\"presentation\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\"><path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M256 8C119.043 8 8 119.083 8 256c0 136.997 111.043 248 248 248s248-111.003 248-248C504 119.083 392.957 8 256 8zm0 110c23.196 0 42 18.804 42 42s-18.804 42-42 42-42-18.804-42-42 18.804-42 42-42zm56 254c0 6.627-5.373 12-12 12h-88c-6.627 0-12-5.373-12-12